WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:04.040
SCP-096 Vs SCP-204.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:09.500
They say that SCP-096 always catches its prey,
but could the strength of The Protector finally

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:10.639
stop it at the door?

00:00:10.639 --> 00:00:11.839
Let’s find out.

00:00:11.839 --> 00:00:17.410
SCP-096 is a relentless and almost indestructible
killing machine that doesn’t even leave

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:19.340
traces of its victims left.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.529
Nothing seems to be able to even slow it down.

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:27.720
SCP-204 is a cloud of deadly, self-replicating
nanites that recharge by feeding on living

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:32.550
flesh, are able to condense into a powerful
physical form, and will do anything to protect

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.489
the child they are assigned to.

00:00:34.489 --> 00:00:38.340
However, we think 096 would still narrowly
win this one.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:44.989
Unlike 096, 204’s condensed form is vulnerable
to conventional damage - which 096 can dish

00:00:44.989 --> 00:00:51.530
out in spades - and 096 would likely regenerate
flesh faster than 204 could reliably eat it.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.969
The Protector’s host child may sadly be
doomed on this one…

